        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$L$ only: 5; $S$ only: 2; $I$ only: 1; $L$ and $S$ only: 1; $L$ and $I$ only: 1; $S$ and $I$ only: 2; all three: 2; outside: 1.",
          "worked": "Place 5 in $L$ only, 1 in $I$ only and 2 in the centre. Find the remaining regions by subtraction:\n$$\\begin{align*}\nn(L\\cap S\\cap I')&=3-2=1\\\\\nn(L\\cap I\\cap S')&=9-5-1-2=1\\\\\nn(S\\cap I\\cap L')&=6-1-1-2=2\\\\\nn(S\\cap L'\\cap I')&=7-1-2-2=2\\\\\nn((L\\cup S\\cup I)')&=15-(5+2+1+1+1+2+2)=1.\n\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p18-q22-a-solution-diagram",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 18 p18-q22-a-solution-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line width=0.8pt,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[black] (-2.3,-1.9) rectangle (2.3,2.45);\n\\draw[black] (0,1) circle[radius=1.25];\n\\draw[black] (-0.85,-0.4) circle[radius=1.25];\n\\draw[black] (0.85,-0.4) circle[radius=1.25];\n\\node at (-0.4,1.9) {$L$};\n\\node at (-1.65,0.05) {$S$};\n\\node at (1.65,0.05) {$I$};\n\\node at (0,1.45) {$5$};\n\\node at (-1.2,-0.85) {$2$};\n\\node at (1.2,-0.85) {$1$};\n\\node at (-0.65,0.55) {$1$};\n\\node at (0.65,0.55) {$1$};\n\\node at (0,-0.95) {$2$};\n\\node at (0,0.15) {$2$};\n\\node at (2,-1.6) {$1$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
